SUMMARY:Plein Air Watercolor Landscapes: A Day at Jack London Park
DESCRIPTION:Spend a day immersed in plein air watercolor landscape painting while taking in the sweeping vistas of Jack London State Historic Park. Participants will explore both watercolor technique and the core principles of landscape painting\, including composition\, color temperature\, and atmospheric perspective. Learn to create movement and depth in your painting\, and gain a new appreciation for the beauty of your surroundings through the process of close observation and careful rendering.\nWe’ll start the class with quick thumbnail sketches\, then select one composition to focus on throughout the day. Through demonstration and individual instruction\, you’ll learn color mixing and watercolor technique while building your painting step by step.\nBring a picnic lunch to enjoy while taking a break\, and a lightweight folding chair if you have one. Otherwise seating is at picnic tables and park benches or on the ground. All other materials are provided.\nAfter the workshop\, you’re invited to continue exploring the park—take a hike\, visit the museum\, or stroll to the evocative ruins of the Wolf House.\nAll levels of experience are welcome!\nNote: $10 per vehicle entry fee to the park is NOT included in class fee.
URL:https://golocal.coop/event/plein-air-watercolor-landscapes-a-day-at-jack-london-park/
LOCATION:Jack London State Historic Park\, 2400 London Ranch Rd.\, Glen Ellen\, CA
CATEGORIES:Art,Recreation
GEO:38.35681;-122.54092
